    "rationale": "Biallelic NR1H4 loss causes farnesoid X receptor deficiency, a severe low-GGT progressive familial intrahepatic cholestasis. FXR normally coordinates bile-acid homeostasis and promotes expression of transport programs including BSEP; loss can therefore reduce BSEP expression despite an intact ABCB11 coding sequence. Strongest alternative resolved: ABCB11/BSEP deficiency is also a low-GGT PFIC, but the stem specifically shows absent FXR with reduced BSEP despite no pathogenic ABCB11 variant and persistently high alpha-fetoprotein; that pattern resolves the case to NR1H4/FXR deficiency."
